From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:21:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll-unix: port signal_arm64_ios.c onto wine-11.18 thread
 data; iOS-aware is_emulated_code

Upstream's diff applied hunk-wise (46 of 57), rejects resolved by hand. The
dispatcher asm is upstream's; signal handlers pass the thread data through;
the iOS segv/ill/bus/trap handlers stay. signal_set_full_context takes
upstream's cooperative suspend and keeps the iOS KiUserEmulationDispatcher
bounce, clearing RESTORE_FLAGS_EMULATION so a resume does not bounce twice.
usr1_handler does not rebuild the syscall frame inside a dispatcher prologue
(sigreturn clears x18 on iOS). is_emulated_code goes by the current
pseudo-process's own EcCodeBitMap and never counts a JIT-pool pc.

Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 403 ++++++++++++++++++++--------
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c      |  18 ++
 2 files changed, 304 insertions(+), 117 deletions(-)

